  "result": "The feature GOAL document is complete. Here's my summary:\n\n**CHANGED:** `docs/feature/00-goal.md` (created)\n\n**What it covers:**\n\nThe document plans F2 — Team workflows for work items — at one level of planning (feature → work packages). It builds on the existing work-item infrastructure (migrations 0046/0047, `src/mem_mcp/mindmap/work_items.py`, the `mindmap_work_*` MCP tools, the web handler `src/mem_mcp/web/handlers/mindmaps.py`, and the web board at `web/app/mindmaps/[key]`).\n\n**Key design decisions captured:**\n\n1. **Data model** — Four new team-scoped tables (`work_item_workflows`, `work_item_workflow_stages`, `work_item_workflow_transitions`, `work_item_signoffs`) + two schema hooks (`memory_maps.workflow_id`, `work_items.stage_id`). The `stage_id` column is the source of truth when a workflow is active; the legacy `status` CHECK (0046:48) remains as the backward-compatible fallback. Stage removal uses `fallback_stage_id` to prevent stranding items.\n\n2. **Rules** — `validate_and_apply_transition` delegates to the existing hardcoded path when no workflow is set, or validates against the team's workflow when one is active. Sign-ups are collected in `work_item_signoffs` and the move only completes when enough valid sign-ups exist.\n\n3. **Backward compatibility** — Zero data backfill; existing rows stay `NULL` and use the existing `TRANSITIONS` dict.\n\n4. **Auth** — Reuses existing permissions (`TEAM_MANAGE_SETTINGS` for workflow definition, `TEAM_WRITE_MEMORY` for moves/sign-ups, `TEAM_READ_MEMORY` for reads) and the `safe_current_tenant_id()` RLS pattern.\n\n5. **Work packages** — WP0 (migration, exclusive) → WP1 (domain/service) → WP2 (MCP tools) → WP3 (web API) → WP4 (web UI board) → WP5 (verification). The JSON block at the end validates as well-formed JSON with 6 packages.\n\n**Not done:** No code was written (per the task constraint). This is the planning document only.",
